// The build reads every suite from one dated snapshot.debian.org timestamp
// (iso/auto/config, ADR-0002). trixie-security's Release carries a
// Valid-Until a few days after that date, so apt would reject the snapshot
// as stale on any later build. The signature and every hash are still
// checked. A replayed older Release is caught only for the packages the hook
// pins (PipeWire, WirePlumber); the rest, kernel included, would install
// from that older signed state unnoticed (ADR-0002, 2026-11-02 amendment).
//
// .conf.chroot, not .conf: live-build removes it before the image is packed,
// so the shipped system keeps expiry checks against the live mirrors.
Acquire::Check-Valid-Until "false";
